{
  "format": 1,
  "description": "A damped pendulum, shown as itself by the pendulum view that comes with the eq.pendulum block (ADR 0016), beside the same pendulum drawn as a scene of layers (ADR 0093: a support, and a rod and bob in a frame turned by the angle, which is measured from straight down, so its frame sits in one turned by -π/2), and its angle over time. The scene's rod is 1 m long, as L is: it draws no parameter. Started at 2 rad it swings well beyond the small-angle range, so its period is longer than 2π√(L/g). Raise c to damp it.",
